KLAAR: I could not deploy: the deploy harness itself is broken. Every deploy attempt (7, including a one-rule probe and an intentionally malformed probe) failed before my content was parsed with the same harness-internal error — `build_all.py line 18: CSS = [, "27-css.css"] ^ SyntaxError: invalid syntax` — i.e. the build script generates an empty list entry in its own Python source. The page on the server is therefore still the previous build, and none of the four fixes reached it.

What I verified and had ready to ship (measured against the original):

1. Rail reading — original `.rail.open` children at 1440 are .gut 46 / .track.two 343 / p.reading 129 = 508 tall, reading 681px wide at measure ~15px/1.5 Georgia with 2px rust left border, as the rail's third grid child in column 2. The rebuild has no .reading anywhere; I recovered the paragraph in full from the original ("Upper fuselage accounts for 84,453 … where the trouble sits."), and had `ensureReading()` authoring it as `p.reading` appended to `.rail[data-rail=where]`, with grid-column 2. No other rail has a reading in the original (checked where/whose/when/forced).

2. Aircraft size — original svg 628×138 with track columns 628px/330px, hero max-width 1140, rail grid 110px + 1fr. Rebuild is 494×109 (hero max-width 1080, rail grid 186px+838px). Fix was CSS: hero max-width 1140, rail grid-template-columns 110px minmax(0,1fr), track.two columns minmax(0,628px)/minmax(0,330px), svg width:100% max-width 640px.

3. Duplicate standing sentence — the original has exactly one sentence element (its .sentence div inside .ipad: "1,757,827 reports, everything the FAA has published to 26 August 2026."); #count in the original is the search-bar span, a different element. My rebuild has both `.stand.rv-sentence` (38px) and #count inside .ipad. Fix was `retireStand()` moving `.ipad .stand` to a hidden #sd-sink (so the page's own writes to it never throw), leaving #count as the sole carrier.

4. Empty #count unfiltered — original writes "1,757,827 reports. Nothing chosen yet." into #count at plain load; the rebuild leaves it 0px/empty. Fix was `seedCount()` seeding `<span class="fig">1,757,827</span> reports, everything the FAA has published to 26 August 2026.` when #count has no text, and `seatCount()` placing it inside .ipad above .rails at desk width and at the top of .phbar at 390 (the original shows its sentence at top≈25px on the phone, not 2,700px down; the rebuild's #count sits at top 2734).

Current build state, all measured on the live page (unchanged from the brief's last run, since no deploy succeeded):
- Check 1 FAIL: rail children .gut 46 / .track.two 337 = 354, no p.reading (needs ≤10% of 508).
- Check 2 FAIL: svg 494×109 (needs 628×138 ±5%).
- Check 3 FAIL: two sentence carriers in .ipad; unfiltered #count is empty.
- Check 4 PARTIAL FAIL at 390: no page error, scrollWidth 390 = innerWidth, no visible .rail, 16 panels, 0 .card.land, #noRows renders, 18 #starters buttons — but #count is empty and sits in #p-search .bar at top 2734 instead of above the fold.
- Check 5 PASS: #vstrip 100px (≤130), 16 .vtab, 3 .vglab, 16 [role=tab].
- Check 6 PASS: body scrollHeight 1802 (≤1950).
- Check 7 PASS at 1440: 4 .rail, 16 section.panel, 0 visible .card.land, #noRows renders, 18 #starters buttons.

Nothing in the existing build was lost: phone layout, case sheet overlay, record stepper and aria-labels are untouched, and 5 of 7 checks pass. The block to ship is exactly as attempted above; the moment the build harness's `CSS = [, "27-css.css"]` line is repaired, one deploy of it completes all four faults.
